    "raw_html": "<div id=\"question-122151\" class=\"question\"><div class=\"questionHeader\"><span class=\"questionNumber\">11.</span><a class=\"questionKP\" href=\"/topics/161#5086\">Applying the Rules of Sum and Product With Letter and Digits</a><span class=\"helpButton\" questionid=\"122151\">?</span></div><div class=\"questionText\"><p>The seats in a certain theater are labeled with an ordered combination of <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"116\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c33\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> possible characters, as shown below:</p>\n<table align=\"center\" style=\"border: 1px solid black; margin: auto; margin-bottom: 4mm; margin-top: 4mm\" rules=\"all\" cellpadding=\"10\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<td width=\"50\" style=\"text-align:center\">Letter</td>\n<td width=\"50\" style=\"text-align:center\">Letter</td>\n<td width=\"50\" style=\"text-align:center\">Digit</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p>Here,</p>\n<ul>\n<li><p>the first \"Letter\" can be any of the following: N, S, E, W.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>the second \"Letter\" can be any capital from A-J (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"117\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> in total), and</p>\n</li>\n<li><p>each \"Digit\" can be any integer between <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"118\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c30\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>-<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"119\" style=\"font-size: 119.4%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c39\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c2E\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9.</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>How many possible ordered combinations are there?</p>\n</div><div class=\"answerDetails\"><div class=\"questionDifficulty difficultyModerate\">M</div><span class=\"answerCreated\">Mon, Oct 5th @ 7:42 AM</span><span class=\"answerDetailsSeparator\">|</span><span class=\"timeElpased\">Elapsed: 1:07</span><span class=\"answerResult\"><span style=\"color: red;\">Incorrect</span></span></div></div>",
